WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Lymph node: capsule, subcapsular sinus, cortical follicles and a deeper medulla.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Spleen: arteriole-associated white-pulp islands within red pulp, not cortex and medulla.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Thymus: incomplete lobules with cortical regions, connected medulla and Hassall corpuscles.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Pause and predict: does a germinal centre alone identify a lymph node?

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.000
No. Combine at least two landmarks and consider which parts the section omits.
